#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8d25cc6-d64f-55e9-8ca4-c04105e01075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364601} {:answer/id #uuid "90453a3a-fc31-5a46-a016-ea3269196bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364602} {:answer/id #uuid "dc710635-5cf0-58be-a70a-d93edbd652dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24(\\sqrt{3}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364603} {:answer/id #uuid "7a622241-5df4-50d5-9447-5cb7979bf5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12(\\sqrt{3}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364604} {:answer/id #uuid "a157230c-ea16-5ad9-9950-c74921a7dd88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\sqrt{3}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc710635-5cf0-58be-a70a-d93edbd652dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24(\\sqrt{3}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364603} :answer-field/id #uuid "7490fd5c-74ef-59af-945c-78603596dcf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3e328fe-736e-5356-b9c9-6e5d01ab2fb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161276" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{3},\\,{e}^{2}\\le y\\le {e}^{5},\\,0\\le z\\le 4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{3}]\\times [{e}^{2},{e}^{5}]\\times [0,4]$ is a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z & =[\\operatorname{tan}⁡x]_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}\\cdot {[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\cdot (5-2)\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\cdot 3\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =24(\\sqrt{3}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d428cf90-7455-53cd-a734-12adbacf3f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364608} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9a2965-8003-5843-8446-81ce630055cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364609} {:answer/id #uuid "332deba6-4911-5fb2-a185-a5b27ed79770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364610} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0dda4b-ca24-55d6-931d-b79b44779a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364611} {:answer/id #uuid "33464de5-eeaf-5f1b-a561-39b377c89dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f0dda4b-ca24-55d6-931d-b79b44779a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364611} :answer-field/id #uuid "5675ef25-4591-5230-bcc4-94fe0e3407cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73d193b7-b76c-51ef-bc22-10cbc20da8cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161279" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,5\\le z\\le 7}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\times [0,1]\\times [5,7]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{5}^{7}\\frac{1}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{5}^{7}\\frac{1}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}z & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{3}^{y-1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-4)]_{5}^{7} \\\\  & =(-0+\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2ef00c-10eb-5571-baea-a9225476dc70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364615} {:answer/id #uuid "a00ba570-675c-55f3-bd57-552bbecc21c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364616} {:answer/id #uuid "e99b9aa6-42c5-51f0-ab37-281781c669d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364617} {:answer/id #uuid "03ed23cc-46a4-5b01-ad52-94e9e238e490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364618} {:answer/id #uuid "1bebea91-bc29-559f-b331-5a9e6d54aa3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bebea91-bc29-559f-b331-5a9e6d54aa3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364619} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaff2740-5411-5502-9b3a-1d86c5d6869d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2f2caf16-d1bb-5667-87e0-25c7b5604d46" :question/math-academy-id "q-161369" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $x,$ and then $z,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-1\\le z\\le 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $x,$ and then $z,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dy]dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{2}zy+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]_{y=1}^{y=3}\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}z(3-1)+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-0)\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}z+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dx\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}z+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}2z{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dx]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{2}{3}\\,z{x}^{3}+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}\\,z(8-0)+(2-0)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{16}{3}\\,z+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{16}{3}z+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dz & ={[\\frac{8}{3}{z}^{2}+2z\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]}_{z=-1}^{z=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}(1-1)+2(1-(-1))\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ffe1951-4f77-5409-bcc7-f42b39234d12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364622} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c84677-09fd-5b94-9ce1-2c957c13f7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364623} {:answer/id #uuid "d8426022-84f7-5f1e-a0e8-bd77259efabd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364624} {:answer/id #uuid "88d5ec8d-4bbd-5cbd-bcd0-a6572798942f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364625} {:answer/id #uuid "d16de6ce-f022-5fd9-a5bd-f4a3287a9389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d16de6ce-f022-5fd9-a5bd-f4a3287a9389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364626} :answer-field/id #uuid "c879a12b-271a-5d66-9053-8a5ffa9758d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fa9615c9-2f4c-558d-98ca-9888f1aa6991" :question/math-academy-id "q-161371" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y+z)]_{0}^{\\pi }\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z+\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z+0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]_{z=0}^{z=\\pi }\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(0-1) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79d74311-7572-5aec-a4c8-ad95a32d6d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364629} {:answer/id #uuid "dea85c0b-f5f7-5feb-b79d-b540f1ead0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364630} {:answer/id #uuid "a4122072-ec99-58ca-a3bc-0d766f458a6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364631} {:answer/id #uuid "aed6811c-cc1d-5ad9-8cb6-21ff718624ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364632} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9eec37-acea-52d0-a4a9-b37ed25f7c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4122072-ec99-58ca-a3bc-0d766f458a6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364631} :answer-field/id #uuid "759db459-2786-5a1e-8f86-e3fb671492bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "30d4472d-d7f5-5b7c-903c-9b27f7371d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-161373" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{2}+(3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3})x]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(9-0)+(3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3})(3-0)\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}9+9{y}^{2}+12{z}^{3}\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}9+9{y}^{2}+12{z}^{3}\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}9+12{z}^{3}+9{y}^{2}\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(9+12{z}^{3})y+3{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9+12{z}^{3})(2-0)+3(8-0)\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}18+24{z}^{3}+24\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}42+24{z}^{3}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}42+24{z}^{3}\\,dz & =[42z+6{z}^{4}]_{z=0}^{z=1} \\\\  & =42(1-0)+6(1-0) \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
